PATCH 646: shared mutable CPU/system/physical memory for device and IRQ consumers.

Original core_normal.cpp Fetchb reads CS:EIP after the trace/clock boundary.
The reached 23c4 dispatch has no cached linear page65538 on entry; its first
opcode links physical page307. The previous translated fetch charged the
clock but omitted this memory operation. Both targets matched all CPU/RAM
words while retaining nine links instead of the original ten at caller77ff.
Perform the actual opcode read through the same bus as data and guest RET.
Remaining encoded operands are translated from the recovered assembly in
644/645; this is not a general instruction decoder or arbitrary-code proof.

The actual1280/23c4/133a assembly keeps all prior byte/word/dword, segment,
flag and CALL/RET contracts. The only typed carrier is now FistCpuRam,
referencing the complete37-word CPU and21-word system state, physical RAM,
providers, first-MB/A20 and mutable linked cache. Descriptor loads, TSS
busy-descriptor stores, hardware IRQ and IRET use this same owner. No synthetic
system fields, identity map or all-writable RAM fallback is introduced.
Original paging.cpp InitPage, PAGING_LinkPage/MapPage/ClearTLB and original
RAM/ROMPageHandler and VGA_Map/ChainedVGA providers back the shared helper.
Normal MIXED/386FAST reached present-page paths set actual PDE/PTE access
and dirty bits. Physical page-table operations bypass logical handlers,
including ROM. Original Descriptor::Save uses two mem_writed calls, not
eight bytes: CPU_LTR through a chained VGA descriptor reaches the old error
even when all58 CPU/system words and complete RAM still match. The actual
recorded callback widths and whole-width fastmem replication reject it.
Logical same-page accesses preserve handler widths; only
cross-page accesses split bytes. Chained VGA preserves planar addresses
and whole-width first-line replication in fastmem.

Source captures keep actual provider/cache and complete2MiB/4MiB VGA inputs
at each selected full-RAM boundary. The existing complete original output,
CPU/code/time and RAM owners are reused unchanged; only added metadata is
removed from their view. Tests compare all58 words, complete16MiB RAM,
the entire observed linked cache and all VGA storage on both targets.
Cold bootstrap, device default/control and existing thin PIC budgets use
real captured system state. Other architectures/providers/fault/task/V86,
actual outer77e2/op6c transport, timer handler execution, first817, final
mixedPCM and full application parity remain open.
